{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Gerrit 2868 LLM-Review +1 advisory disposition — accepted with no patch change after direct falsification. The advisory claimed Terraform templatefile turns source `$$VAR` into `$VAR`. A scoped Terraform console check at the reviewed tree returned source `\"$$VAR\"` as `\"$$VAR\"`, while source `\"$${VAR}\"` returned `\"${VAR}\"`. Terraform escaping applies to the interpolation opener, not a brace-less double dollar. Bash therefore would interpret the retained `$$VAR` as PID plus literal `VAR`, exactly as the condensed header says. The independently reviewed exact SHA aabbed82e2ff97aab8e3e3dcdcba373e6c8897c2 remains unchanged; no semantic or documentation gap is deferred."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788926163548077001,"uuid":"d0713eea-bae2-4652-88eb-f80189e2c2d4"}